MAE and S-MAE feature integration\n\n**Statistics**:\n- Lines of code: ~800\n- Classes: 8\n- Well-commented and documented\n\n### 3. Configuration File\n**File**: `libcity/config/model/traffic_state_pred/STDMAE.json` (Already exists)\n\n**Status**: Verified and compatible with implementation\n\n**Key Parameters**:\n- Architecture: embed_dim=96, num_heads=4, encoder_depth=4\n- Backend: blocks=4, layers=2, skip_channels=256\n- Training: learning_rate=0.0005, batch_size=32\n\n### 4. Documentation\n**Files Created**:\n1. `documentation/STDMAE_ADAPTATION_REPORT.md` - Detailed adaptation report\n2. `documentation/STDMAE_FILES_SUMMARY.md` - File structure and overview\n3. `documentation/STDMAE_CONFIG_PARAMS.md` - Parameter reference guide\n4. `documentation/STDMAE_COMPLETE_SUMMARY.md` - This file\n\n### 5. Testing\n**File**: `test_stdmae_import.py`\n\n**Test Coverage**:\n- ✅ Import validation\n- ✅ Component imports\n- ✅ Model initialization\n- ✅ Forward pass\n- ✅ Loss calculation\n\n## Architecture Summary\n\n### Data Flow\n```\nInput Data: [B, T, N, C]\n    ↓\nT-MAE Encoder (Temporal) → [B, N, P, 96]\nS-MAE Encoder (Spatial)  → [B, N, P, 96]\n    ↓\nConcatenate → [B, N, P, 192]\nExtract Last Patch → [B, N, 192]\n    ↓\nGraphWaveNet Backend (with short history)\n    ↓\nOutput: [B, T_out, N, 1]\n```\n\n### Model Components\n1. **T-MAE**: Temporal masked autoencoder\n   - Patches: 12 timesteps each\n   - Embedding: 96-dimensional\n   - Frozen parameters (pre-trained)\n\n2. **S-MAE**: Spatial masked autoencoder\n   - Patches: 12 nodes each (spatial masking)\n   - Embedding: 96-dimensional\n   - Frozen parameters (pre-trained)\n\n3. **GraphWaveNet**: Spatial-temporal modeling\n   - Input: Short-term history + combined MAE features\n   - Layers: 4 blocks × 2 layers (configurable)\n   - Trainable parameters: ~2M (approximate)\n\n## Adaptation Details\n\n### Key Changes from Original\n\n| Aspect | Original | LibCity Version |\n|--------|----------|-----------------|\n| Class Base