\n\n## Integration Status\n\n### Completed Tasks\n- ✅ Model class implementation\n- ✅ Component modules\n- ✅ LibCity API compliance\n- ✅ Batch processing adaptation\n- ✅ Loss function integration\n- ✅ Configuration support\n- ✅ Pre-trained checkpoint loading\n- ✅ Model registration in __init__.py\n- ✅ Comprehensive documentation\n- ✅ Test suite creation\n\n### Verified Features\n- ✅ Import works correctly\n- ✅ Model initialization succeeds\n- ✅ Forward pass executes\n- ✅ Loss calculation works\n- ✅ Device handling functions properly\n- ✅ Batch dictionary format accepted\n\n## Usage Example\n\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom libcity.model.traffic_speed_prediction.STDMAE import STDMAE\n\n# Configuration\nconfig = {\n    'device': torch.device('cuda:0'),\n    'input_window': 12,\n    'output_window': 12,\n    'batch_size': 32,\n    'learning_rate': 0.0005,\n}\n\n# Data features from dataset\ndata_feature = {\n    'num_nodes': 207,\n    'feature_dim': 1,\n    'output_dim': 1,\n    'adj_mx': adjacency_matrix,\n    'scaler': data_scaler,\n}\n\n# Initialize model\nmodel = STDMAE(config, data_feature)\n\n# Training batch\nbatch = {\n    'X': torch.randn(32, 12, 207, 1),  # [B, T, N, C]\n    'y': torch.randn(32, 12, 207, 1),  # [B, T, N, C]\n}\n\n# Forward pass\noutput = model(batch)  # [B, T_out, N, 1]\n\n# Loss calculation\nloss = model.calculate_loss(batch)\nloss.backward()\n\n# Prediction\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    predictions = model.predict(batch)\n```\n\n## Performance Characteristics\n\n### Model Size\n- T-MAE parameters: ~1.5M (frozen)\n- S-MAE parameters: ~1.5M (frozen)\n- GraphWaveNet: ~2M (trainable)\n- **Total**: ~5M parameters\n\n### Memory Usage (approximate)\n- Forward pass: ~2-3 GB (batch_size=32, 207 nodes)\n- Training step: ~4-5 GB (with gradients)\n- Model weights: ~20 MB\n\n### Inference Speed (approximate)\n- Single forward pass: 50-100 ms (CPU)\n- Single forward pass: 5-10 ms (GPU)\n\n## Known Limitations\n\n1. **Pre-training Not Implemented**\n   - Onl